Time Series Regression code
====================

from statsmodels.tsa.ar_model import AutoReg

# Train Test Split (Series)
X_train = data1[:10]
X_test = data1[10:]

# Model Training
model = AutoReg(X_train, lags=1)
model_fit = model.fit()

# Prediction
y_pred = model_fit.predict(
    len(X_train),
    len(data1)-1
)

====================

| Code                                                     | Description                                                                                 |
| -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `from statsmodels.tsa.ar_model import AutoReg`           | Imports the AutoReg model from the Statsmodels library.                                     |
| `X_train = data1[:10]`                                   | Selects the first 10 observations as training data.                                         |
| `X_test = data1[10:]`                                    | Selects the remaining observations as testing data.                                         |
| `model = AutoReg(X_train, lags=1)`                       | Creates an AutoRegressive model using 1 previous value (lag = 1) to predict the next value. |
| `model_fit = model.fit()`                                | Trains (fits) the AutoReg model on the training data.                                       |
| `y_pred = model_fit.predict(len(X_train), len(data1)-1)` | Predicts values from the end of the training data up to the last record in the dataset.     |
| `lags=1`                                                 | Uses one previous time step to make predictions.                                            |
| `y_pred`                                                 | Stores the predicted values generated by the model.                                         |

