ML Regression code

--------------
loaded_model = pickle.load(open("finalized_model_Mul_linear.sav",'rb'))
result = loaded_model.predict([[2344,345,435,0,1]])

--------------

| Code                                         | Purpose                                                      |
| -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `pickle.load(...)`                           | Loads the saved Machine Learning model from the `.sav` file. |
| `loaded_model.predict([[2344,345,435,0,1]])` | Predicts the output using the given input features.          |
| `result`                                     | Stores the predicted value.                                  |

==================

| Time Series Regression                                       | Machine Learning Regression            |
| ------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------- |
| Training and Test should be **series** (chronological order) | Training and Test should be **random** |
| `AutoReg()` model used                                       | Saved ML model loaded using `pickle`   |
| Uses previous time values for prediction                     | Uses feature values for prediction     |
| `predict(len(X_train), len(data1)-1)`                        | `predict([[2344,345,435,0,1]])`        |


